---
// What LaserTouchOne is cleared for, word for word, and what "cleared" means.
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/site/PageHero.astro';
import Icon from '../components/site/Icon.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/site/CtaBand.astro';
import { INDICATION, SITE } from '../site.config.js';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema.js';
const PDF = 'https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/cdrh_docs/pdf10/K100116.pdf';
---
<SiteLayout schema={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'FDA clearance', path: '/fda-clearance' }])]}>
  <PageHero title="LaserTouchOne’s FDA clearance" lead="Exactly what the FDA cleared LaserTouchOne for, and what “cleared” means." />

  <section class="section section--tight-top">
    <div class="container split split--reverse">
      <div class="fda-card">
        <span class="icon-badge icon-badge--lg"><Icon name="file" size={24} /></span>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Clearance</dt><dd>510(k) K100116</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Cleared</dt><dd>April 15, 2010</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Use</dt><dd>Over the counter, no prescription</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Technology</dt><dd>670 nm low-level laser + electrical stimulation (FDA over-the-counter TENS category)</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Maker</dt><dd>{SITE.manufacturer}, Scottsdale, AZ</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <a class="link-arrow" href={PDF} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the FDA document <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
      </div>
      <div class="split__copy">
        <h2 class="h2">The cleared indication, word for word</h2>
        <blockquote class="quote-card">
          <p>“{INDICATION}”</p>
          <footer>FDA clearance K100116, indications for use. <a href={PDF} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the document</a></footer>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Everything we say about LaserTouchOne stays inside this wording.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Cleared, not approved: what’s the difference?</h2>
        <p>The FDA reviews medical devices in different ways depending on their risk. For a device like LaserTouchOne, the maker submits a “510(k)” showing the device is substantially equivalent to devices already legally on the market. When the FDA agrees, the device is “cleared” for the specific uses listed. “Approved” is a different process, used mainly for higher-risk devices, so “FDA-cleared” is the correct term here. The clearance covers the uses above, not every kind of pain.</p>
        <h2>What “over the counter” means</h2>
        <p>LaserTouchOne was cleared for over-the-counter sale, so you can buy it without a prescription. Read the user manual before use, and talk to your doctor about your pain, especially if it is new, severe or unexplained.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Questions about the clearance?" text="Text or email us and a real person will help." />
</SiteLayout>
